reliability of a body knowledge instrument in school-age children</article-title><source>Matern Child Nurs J</source><year>1994</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7967751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hadlow</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pitts</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The understanding of common health terms by doctors, nurses and patients</article-title><source>Social Science &#x00026; Medicine</source><year>1991</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2014414</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0277-9536(91)90059-L</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rashid</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jagger</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patients' knowledge of anatomical location of major organs within the human body: a comparison between Asians and non-Asians</article-title><source>Fam Pract</source><year>1996</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>450</fpage><lpage>454</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8902514</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/fampra/13.5.450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibbs</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibbs</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Henrich</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient understanding of commonly used medical vocabulary</article-title><source>J Fam Pract</source><year>1987</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>176</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3612043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pledger</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Doctor-patient communication: is patient knowledge of medical terminology improving?</article-title><source>Health Commun</source><year>1993</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1207/s15327027hc0502_2</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>